====== PC Engines APU2 ======
The APU2 is a small [[docs:techref:instructionset:x86_64|x86_64]] single board computer. It will easily route/packet filter a one Gigabit WAN. IPsec/VPN may drop that number a wee bit, the CPU has AES-NI acceleration, use AES-GCM for performance.

APU system boards were designed and manufactured by PC Engines in Taiwan.

Boards are based on [[http://www.cpu-world.com/CPUs/Puma/AMD-G-Series%20GX-412TC.html|AMD Embedded G series GX-412TC]] low (6 to 12W) power consumption CPUs.
APU boards and associated accessories are readily available from [[https://pcengines.ch/order.htm|resellers]] across Europe and North America.

Tested wifi options include the PC Engines supplied [[https://pcengines.ch/wle900vx.htm|WLE900VX]], [[https://pcengines.ch/wle600vx.htm|WLE600VX]] (both ath10k, 802.11ac/a/b/g/n) and full feature support via [[https://pcengines.ch/wle200nx.htm|WLE200NX]] (ath9k, 802.11a/b/g/n) miniPCI express radio cards.

The APU2 series is available in a number of models - [[toh:pcengines:apu3|PC Engines APU 3]], [[toh:pcengines:apu4|PC Engines APU 4]], APU5, APU6 and APU7.

These differ in how one of the 5 PCIe x1 interfaces is routed as follows:

APU2 - PCIe interfaces 0-2 are connected to the three Ethernet controllers, PCIe 3 connects to the MiniPCIe port J14 and PCIe 4 to J13\\
[[toh:pcengines:apu3|APU3]] - PCIe interfaces 0-2 as above, PCIe 3 connects to the MiniPCIe port J16 and PCIe 4 to the card edge connector\\
[[toh:pcengines:apu4|APU4]] - PCIe interfaces 0-2 as above, PCIe 3 connects to the MiniPCIe port J15 and PCIe 4 to the fourth Ethernet chip\\
APU6 - Essentially as [[toh:pcengines:apu4|APU4]] but the fourth Ethernet controller is an i210CS connected to the SFP port\\

[[toh:pcengines:apu3|APU3]] and [[toh:pcengines:apu4|APU4]] boards only support one WiFi module though they will support two 3G/4G LTE modules - they are normally described as being "optimised" for LTE modems. 5G modems could be used (the T99W175 certainly works) but these typically use a PCIe interface in an M.2 "B" key format. There isn't room for a MiniPCIe to M.2 adapter as the Ethernet ports get in the way but one can be connected using a MiniPCIe extender. Make sure an adapter which routes the PCIe connections is used, many are USB only intended for 3G/4G modems.

APU5 and APU7 models also existed but were never sold commercially - APU5 was a custom design and APU7 was a prototype using i225 Ethernet controllers.

Unfortunately the GX-412TC has been out of production since the summer of 2023, PC Engines acquired enough stock to continue manufacturing until June 2024 but after this date no more boards have been manufactured. At the time of writing (April 2025) I am not aware of any retail outlet which still has new stock of apu2 boards.

